Z||000002||Fiero_24||07-09-2001||11:39 PM||||Go with Nitrous.  I have a post saved at work about a guy with NOS on his car.  Here is a linl to start you out with.  Never buy a kit you have not researched.  I am building a 2.8 from scratch with NOS.  50hp increase.  <A HREF="http://www.nosnitrous.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.nosnitrous.com/</A> <P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT||||reg||14
Z||000003||Loki||07-10-2001||12:26 AM||||Look for 1FST2M6   He knows all about it  and also has used NOS brand and didnt like it..Belive NitrousExpress (I think) is the one he recomends...But ask for him<BR><P>------------------<BR>Loki<BR>ICQ# 16477998||||reg||1
Z||000004||1FST2M6||07-10-2001||08:43 AM||||YOU RANG&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; <P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/006347.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/006347.html</A> <P>You dont' NEED anything but the kit.. however.. and MSD 6a or AL. a decent coil and new plugs and fuel injection service can't hurt. I'm using NGK ur5 plugs, headers and 2.5" exhasut.  with the 75 hp jetting, i'm making over 100extra hp and not running lean. i've run it on Engineered Performances Dynojet model 248C with their Competition Data systems O2 stream running and the leanest it gets is 12.1:1. the EGTs are decent too.. about 990* but thats not too bad. (the egts and air fuel don't quiet match and we're working on that.)<P>this is my dyno sheet under the fog. <P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fst-schoolgirl.jpg">   <P>my off nitrous numbers are 154hp and 168lbft the kit i had before on an 86 SE 4spd 4:10. was a dry kit and it didn't make ANYhp.. but hella torque. having a daily driver shot of only 164hp and 253lbft. the new wet kit is exponentially better. and was just as easy to install. took about 4 hours trying to hide the wiring and make it look decent.<P>get a hold of John Stewart at <A HREF="http://www.nitrouswarehouse.com" TARGET=_blank>www.nitrouswarehouse.com</A>  he'll get you a killer kit than go buy stock in a tire store...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P>Happy foggin! <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fsthydrantsig.jpg">           <A HREF="http://www.engineered.net" TARGET=_blank>www.engineered.net</A> <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 07-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||b lo 0||07-10-2001||01:28 PM||||Hey 1FST-me, your local Atlanta area pest again-long time no see!  Anyways, I wanted to know if you would reccomend the wet system on an auto trans with a shift kit?  Lemme know-I'll get Engineered to tune it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> .  Thanks, dude!<P>PS-how'd the noise ordinance ticket turn out?<P>------------------<BR>'85 GT (in progress)  <BR>titled ICE-plates B LO 0 <BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.angelfire.com/ga3/audioimagery/ice.gif">     <BR>Go to <A HREF="http://www.audioimagery.i-p.com" TARGET=_blank>www.audioimagery.i-p.com</A>  !!!<P><A HREF="http://clubs.excite.com/welcome/main?cid=.zXb1DJ1lsCL&aid=22&auth=" TARGET=_blank>Pontiac Fiero Owner's Club</A>-Pics, Videos and More-Or Post your Own||||reg||1
